    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="0871" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–2745</note>
                <head>No. 783<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Political Adviser to the
                        Representative on the European Advisory Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mosely</hi>)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d783-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-27">July 27, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>During the course of the Conference the three Heads of Governments considered and
                    approved the Agreement on Zones of Occupation in Austria and the Administration
                    of the City of Vienna and the Agreement on Control Machinery in Austria,
                    recommended by the European Advisory Commission. Upon approval by the three
                    Governments and the Provisional Government of the French Republic, it was
                    decided to place in effect at once the two Agreements which provide, in the
                    spirit of the Moscow Declaration of November 1, 1943,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d783-f2"/> on Austria, for Allied occupation and control of
                    Austria.</p>
                <p>It is contemplated that a joint statement will be issued shortly regarding the
                    arrangements which have been entered into for the purpose of carrying out the
                    declared policy of establishing a free and independent Austria.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
